<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    Settings, as SettingsCard rows.

    This page was 438 lines of hand-rolled two-column grid-in-border, one copy per row, and every copy was a
    chance for a label to sit a pixel off or an AutomationProperties.Name to be forgotten. SettingsCard is the
    same layout with the keyboard and screen-reader behaviour supplied — Header, Description and a content slot,
    which is exactly the shape every row here already had.

    It is the project's first non-SDK package reference, and it was measured before being taken: a trimmed
    Release publish produces the identical 37 ILLink warnings with and without it, all of them from CsWinRT's
    ABI layer, and the published output is the same size to a tenth of a megabyte. It neither helps nor hinders
    the standing PublishTrimmed work.

    Group rhythm comes from the containers, not from margins on the headers — one StackPanel per group spacing
    its rows, an outer one spacing the groups. That is what finally let GroupHeaderStyle go: it differed from
    the shared section header only by the margin it carried.
-->
<Page
    x:Class="Ripcord_App.Pages.SettingsPage"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
    xmlns:local="using:Ripcord_App.Pages"
    xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
    xmlns:tk="using:CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls"
    Loaded="Page_Loaded"
    mc:Ignorable="d">

    <!--
        RectilinearDistance, not the default overlap rule. MEASURED, not reasoned about — three earlier
        attempts at this were guesses and all three were wrong.

        By default XY focus only considers a candidate that geometrically OVERLAPS the focused element on the
        perpendicular axis. On this page the controls do not line up: the sliders occupy x 776-996, because
        their value readout sits to their right and pushes them left, while every ToggleSwitch occupies
        x 1008-1080. A twelve-pixel gap, so a slider and a toggle have no overlap at all and are invisible to
        each other. Pressing Down on the bitrate slider stepped straight over the adaptive-bitrate toggle to
        the next ComboBox, which is wide enough to overlap.

        Projection was tried first and could not have worked: it projects the focused element's bounds along
        the direction of travel, which still requires perpendicular overlap. RectilinearDistance ranks
        candidates by distance instead and needs no overlap, which is what "the next control down" means to a
        person reading a settings list.

        On the container, not as XYFocusUp/Down element references — the plan's rule, and the reason is
        visible right here: the exact alignment that broke this is the kind of thing markup changes silently.
    -->
    <ScrollViewer Padding="24,16,24,24">
        <StackPanel
            MaxWidth="820"
            Spacing="24"
            XYFocusDownNavigationStrategy="RectilinearDistance"
            XYFocusUpNavigationStrategy="RectilinearDistance">
            <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource TitleTextBlockStyle}" Text="Settings" />

            <!--
                ============ Account ============

                First, because it is the only section that changes what the others can do: signed in, pairing
                stops asking for an account ID and a console that is not on this network can still be woken.
            -->
            <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource RipcordSectionHeaderStyle}" Text="Account" />

                <tk:SettingsCard x:Name="AccountCard" Header="PlayStation Network">
                    <tk:SettingsCard.HeaderIcon>
                        <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE77B;" />
                    </tk:SettingsCard.HeaderIcon>

                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                        <ProgressRing x:Name="AccountBusy" Width="20" Height="20" IsActive="False" />
                        <Button x:Name="SignInButton" Content="Sign in" />
                        <Button x:Name="SignOutButton" Content="Sign out" Visibility="Collapsed" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <!--  Only shown when there is something to say — an error, or the account's console list.  -->
                <InfoBar
                    x:Name="AccountError"
                    IsOpen="False"
                    IsClosable="False"
                    Severity="Warning" />

                <tk:SettingsExpander
                    x:Name="CloudConsolesExpander"
                    Visibility="Collapsed"
                    Header="Consoles on this account"
                    Description="Reported by PlayStation Network, including consoles that aren't on this network.">
                    <tk:SettingsExpander.HeaderIcon>
                        <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE7F4;" />
                    </tk:SettingsExpander.HeaderIcon>
                </tk:SettingsExpander>
            </StackPanel>

            <!--  ============ Video ============  -->
            <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource RipcordSectionHeaderStyle}" Text="Video" />

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="720p60 is the verified-good default. Higher settings need a strong network."
                    Header="Resolution and frame rate">
                    <ComboBox
                        x:Name="ResolutionCombo"
                        MinWidth="180"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Resolution and frame rate" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <!--
                    The slider sits in the content slot with its value beside it rather than under a header,
                    because a number that moves needs to be next to the thing moving it.
                -->
                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="The starting rate. Ripcord lowers it automatically if the network can't keep up."
                    Header="Maximum bitrate">
                    <StackPanel
                        Orientation="Horizontal"
                        Spacing="12"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center">
                        <Slider
                            x:Name="BitrateSlider"
                            MinWidth="220"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Maximum bitrate in megabits per second"
                            Maximum="40"
                            Minimum="2"
                            StepFrequency="1" />
                        <TextBlock
                            x:Name="BitrateValueText"
                            MinWidth="72"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                            Style="{StaticResource BodyStrongTextBlockStyle}" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="Lower the bitrate on packet loss, and on battery or when the device gets hot."
                    Header="Adapt quality automatically">
                    <ToggleSwitch
                        x:Name="AdaptiveToggle"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Adapt quality automatically" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard Description="How the stream is scaled up to fill the window." Header="Image scaling">
                    <ComboBox
                        x:Name="UpscaleCombo"
                        MinWidth="180"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Image scaling" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="Sends the measured delay and packet loss to the console, and asks it for the bitrate Ripcord thinks your connection can carry. Off by default because it is not yet verified against real hardware — turn it on and watch the diagnostics graph to see whether it helps."
                    Header="Tell the console about your connection (experimental)">
                    <ToggleSwitch
                        x:Name="ConnectionQualityToggle"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Tell the console about your connection" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>
            </StackPanel>

            <!--  ============ Graphics device ============  -->
            <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource RipcordSectionHeaderStyle}" Text="Graphics device" />

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="Automatic picks the GPU driving your display, which is usually both the fastest and the most efficient choice for streaming. Takes effect on the next connection."
                    Header="Which GPU to use">
                    <ComboBox
                        x:Name="GpuCombo"
                        MinWidth="180"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Which GPU to use" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <!--  Shown only for the "specific GPU" preference — see SettingsViewModel.AdapterPickerVisible.  -->
                <tk:SettingsCard
                    x:Name="AdapterCard"
                    Header="Specific adapter"
                    Visibility="Collapsed">
                    <ComboBox
                        x:Name="AdapterCombo"
                        MinWidth="280"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Specific graphics adapter" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <InfoBar
                    x:Name="AdapterWarning"
                    IsClosable="False"
                    IsOpen="False"
                    Severity="Warning" />

                <!--
                    HEVC is offered only when a decoder for it exists on this machine, so the option cannot be
                    selected into a session that then fails to start. The Description is written from the
                    view-model, because what it says depends on that answer.
                -->
                <tk:SettingsCard x:Name="CodecCard" Header="Video codec">
                    <ComboBox
                        x:Name="CodecCombo"
                        MinWidth="180"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Video codec" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <!--
                    HDR expands, because the readiness checklist is the reason someone opens it. Four things are
                    needed and only one of them is this toggle, so a user whose picture stays SDR has no way to
                    tell WHICH is missing from a sentence listing them all. Each row reports its own state and,
                    when unmet, says what to do.

                    The console row is deliberately neutral rather than a tick or a cross: whether the PS5 sends
                    HDR cannot be known until a session runs, and a cross for "unknown" reads as a fault the
                    user should go and fix.
                -->
                <tk:SettingsExpander Header="Request HDR">
                    <ToggleSwitch x:Name="HdrToggle" AutomationProperties.Name="Request HDR" />

                    <tk:SettingsExpander.Items>
                        <tk:SettingsCard HorizontalContentAlignment="Left" ContentAlignment="Left">
                            <StackPanel Spacing="6">
                                <StackPanel x:Name="HdrChecklist" Spacing="3" />
                                <TextBlock
                                    x:Name="HdrHelpText"
                                    Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                                    Style="{StaticResource CaptionTextBlockStyle}"
                                    TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                            </StackPanel>
                        </tk:SettingsCard>
                    </tk:SettingsExpander.Items>
                </tk:SettingsExpander>
            </StackPanel>

            <!--  ============ Controls ============  -->
            <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource RipcordSectionHeaderStyle}" Text="Controls" />

                <!--
                    Keyboard input is off by default: with a pad connected there is no reason for stray typing to
                    reach the game, and the default layout overlaps ordinary window shortcuts.
                -->
                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="Off by default — with a pad connected, stray typing has no reason to reach the game."
                    Header="Send keyboard input to the console">
                    <ToggleSwitch
                        x:Name="KeyboardToggle"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Send keyboard input to the console" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard x:Name="KeyBindingsCard" Header="Keys and gamepad mapping">
                    <Button
                        x:Name="KeyBindingsButton"
                        Click="KeyBindings_Click"
                        Content="Configure…" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard x:Name="ExitGestureCard" Header="Leave a stream with the controller">
                    <ComboBox
                        x:Name="ExitGestureCombo"
                        MinWidth="180"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Leave a stream with the controller" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="How far you must push the stick to move between items in Ripcord's own menus."
                    Header="Menu stick sensitivity">
                    <StackPanel
                        Orientation="Horizontal"
                        Spacing="12"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center">
                        <Slider
                            x:Name="DeadzoneSlider"
                            MinWidth="220"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Menu stick sensitivity"
                            Maximum="0.9"
                            Minimum="0.1"
                            StepFrequency="0.05" />
                        <TextBlock
                            x:Name="DeadzoneValueText"
                            MinWidth="72"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                            Style="{StaticResource BodyStrongTextBlockStyle}" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </tk:SettingsCard>
            </StackPanel>

            <!--  ============ Display ============  -->
            <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource RipcordSectionHeaderStyle}" Text="Display" />

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="Hides the title bar and navigation while you play."
                    Header="Full screen when a stream starts">
                    <ToggleSwitch
                        x:Name="FullScreenToggle"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Full screen when a stream starts" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="Confirms when you end a stream, and lets you choose rest mode for that disconnect. Off leaves instantly, using the default below."
                    Header="Ask before disconnecting">
                    <ToggleSwitch
                        x:Name="ConfirmOnDisconnectToggle"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Ask before disconnecting" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="The default answer for rest mode: puts the console into rest when you end the stream, instead of leaving it awake."
                    Header="Rest console when I disconnect">
                    <ToggleSwitch
                        x:Name="RestOnDisconnectToggle"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Rest console when I disconnect" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="Frame rate, latency and packet loss over the video. You can also toggle this with F3 while streaming."
                    Header="Show connection diagnostics">
                    <ToggleSwitch
                        x:Name="DiagnosticsToggle"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Show connection diagnostics" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>

                <tk:SettingsCard
                    Description="Easier to read on a handheld or from across the room."
                    Header="Larger text and controls">
                    <ToggleSwitch
                        x:Name="LargeUiToggle"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Larger text and controls" />
                </tk:SettingsCard>
            </StackPanel>

            <!--  ============ Saved consoles ============  -->
            <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource RipcordSectionHeaderStyle}" Text="Saved consoles" />

                <InfoBar
                    x:Name="CredentialProtectionBar"
                    IsClosable="False"
                    IsOpen="True"
                    Severity="Informational" />
            </StackPanel>
        </StackPanel>
    </ScrollViewer>
</Page>
